Load the style dialog with the signals blocked

QtCurveConfig::setWidgetOptions() writes each input through a setter
that emits. An interlock slot then runs part way through the load. It
reads an input that the loader has not reached yet, and it writes a
value that the configuration does not hold. A stored rounding of max
falls back to extra. A stored pair of GTK button order flags loses one
flag. The unified spin button flag and the custom title bar button
flag go the same way. The next Apply writes each damaged value over
the file.

The load also depends on those signals for the enabled state. An input
whose index does not change emits nothing. The affected inputs keep
the enabled state of the user interface file. They include the colour
button of the combo box, the group box factor, two more colour buttons
and the thin groove box.

Block the signals of every child widget for the whole load. Add
updateEnableStates(), which sets the state of each dependent input
from its master input. The load calls it once at the end, and
updateChanged() calls it for the interactive path, so one function
holds each rule.

The change sits on the branch work/dialog-state of the local tree, as commit 1 of 12.
A new merge request on system/qtcurve takes that branch.

Drop this patch when upstream merges the change.

